---
import { SCIGROUND_DOCS } from '../../data/sciground-docs';
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
---
<PageLayout title="SciGround documentation" description="Start with a design, data, or an existing analysis. Learn how SciGround connects verification, and connect through MCP or API." toc={[]} markdownHref="/docs/index.md" llmsHref="/docs/llms.txt">
  <header class="page-head"><p class="eyebrow">SciGround / Docs</p><h1>A basis you and your AI can check.</h1><p class="standfirst">Understand the verification, find your research workflow, and connect SciGround to the environment you use.</p></header>
  <section class="section"><h2>Find your next step</h2><div class="doc-list">{SCIGROUND_DOCS.map((doc) => <article><h3><a href={`/docs/${doc.slug}/`}>{doc.title}</a></h3><p>{doc.description}</p></article>)}</div></section>
  <section class="section"><h2>For research agents</h2><p>Each guide has an equivalent Markdown version. Discover the appropriate guide from the documentation index before selecting a workflow.</p><p><a href="/docs/llms.txt">Agent discovery index</a> · <a href="/docs/index.md">Markdown documentation index</a></p></section>
  <section class="section"><h2>Earlier nomue artifacts</h2><p>Original package documentation, Protocol references, and examples retain their names, versions, and boundaries. The nomue npm packages are separate from the SciGround connection.</p><p><a href="/docs/nomue/">nomue documentation</a> · <a href="/nomue/">nomue product reference</a> · <a href="/roadmap/">nomue roadmap reference</a></p></section>
</PageLayout>
<style>@layer design { .doc-list article { padding: 1.75rem 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule-faint); } .doc-list h3 { margin-bottom: .6rem; } .doc-list p { margin: 0; } }</style>
